-- Prefer rolling back the application/worker while retaining this compatible
-- additive column. This structural rollback is only for operators who have
-- stopped every new-code reader/writer and backed up first-indexed timestamps.
-- Removing the column loses that derived history; reapply reconstructs a
-- retained-message baseline, which cannot recover earlier first-indexed times when those messages are gone.
ALTER TABLE senders DROP COLUMN first_indexed_at;
